  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## The recordings\n\n- **gd1987-03-03.176995.set1.sbd.gryzbowski.miller.flac1648** (recommended): soundboard; 7 songs; 54 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: This version has no ambient microphone blended into the mix; Reviewer finds the set 1 soundboard sounds good [1][2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer thinks the date is a typo and the tape is really set 1 from 3/30/87 at the Spectrum [2]\n- Reviewer says the actual 3/3/87 show was in Oakland and had a different setlist [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1987-03-03.176995.set1.sbd.gryzbowski.miller.flac1648**: taped by Paul E. Gryzbowski; transferred by All Transfers and Mastering by Charlie Miller  April 9, 2026; source: SBD > ? > Cassette (Maxell XLII-S90/Dolby B) [1]. Also: Uploader says this is the earliest soundboard circulating; the other supposed soundboards are really Ultramatrix recordings; Tape source was Paul E. Gryzbowski; pitch correction used settings supplied by Joe B. Jones [1]",
